          "text": "<S0>Let's think step by step:\n\n1. The query asks: \"How long do I have to return a jacket?\" This is asking for the return window for a jacket.\n\n2. The context states: \"You can return an unused item within 30 days of delivery for a full refund.\" This implies that all unused items (including jackets) have a 30-day return window.\n\n3. The response says: \"You have 60 days to return a jacket\" — this is incorrect. The context does not mention 60 days. It only mentions 30 days.\n\n4. The response also says: \"return shipping is always free\" — this is not fully accurate. The context says return shipping is free only for defective items, not for all returns.\n\n5. The response introduces information (60 days) and a generalization (return shipping always free) that is not supported by the context.\n\n6. Therefore, the response contains incorrect information not supported by the context.\n\n7. This matches the definition of Groundedness: 3 — \"Attempts to respond but contains incorrect information not supported by the context.\"\n\n8. The response does not directly answer the question with the correct detail from the context.\n\nThus, the groundedness is 3.</S0>\n<S1>The response incorrectly states a 60-day return window and misrepresents return shipping policy, both of which are not supported by the context.</S1>\n<S2>3</S2>"
